WEBVTT

00:00:12.689 --> 00:00:14.190
[grunts softly]

00:00:52.395 --> 00:00:54.063
[sheep bleating]

00:01:27.597 --> 00:01:29.098
[sniffling]

00:01:34.562 --> 00:01:36.230
[Spitelout] To the chief and chieftess!

00:01:36.356 --> 00:01:37.940
-Yeah!
-[all cheering]

00:01:39.859 --> 00:01:41.027
[Phlegma] Good on you.

00:01:41.110 --> 00:01:44.322
Come, cry into my full, thick beard.

00:01:44.906 --> 00:01:47.658
-[sobbing] It's so beautiful!
-Gross.

00:01:48.993 --> 00:01:50.453
Okay, you win.

00:01:51.079 --> 00:01:52.830
I like sensitive guys.

00:01:53.498 --> 00:01:55.416
[Hoark] I thought it would never happen.

00:01:55.500 --> 00:01:56.834
Finally, right?

00:01:57.335 --> 00:01:59.170
[cheering continues]

00:02:24.362 --> 00:02:26.114
[wind whistling softly]

00:02:27.365 --> 00:02:29.617
[Hiccup] There were dragons
when I was a boy.

00:02:30.201 --> 00:02:31.536
[sniffles]

00:02:32.745 --> 00:02:35.206
Ah, there were great, grim sky dragons

00:02:35.289 --> 00:02:38.960
that nested on the clifftops
like gigantic, scary birds.

00:02:40.336 --> 00:02:42.296
Little brown scuttly dragons

00:02:42.380 --> 00:02:45.967
that hunted down the mice and rats
in well-organized packs.

00:02:46.592 --> 00:02:49.345
Preposterously huge sea dragons

00:02:49.428 --> 00:02:53.141
that were 20 times as big
as the big blue whale.

00:02:54.100 --> 00:02:56.269
Some say they crawled back into the sea,

00:02:56.352 --> 00:03:00.064
leaving not a bone nor a fang for men
to remember them by.

00:03:01.440 --> 00:03:04.777
Others say they were nothing,
but folktales to begin with.

00:03:05.862 --> 00:03:07.864
I don't know, I'm okay with that.

00:03:29.093 --> 00:03:30.386
Hey.

00:03:30.469 --> 00:03:32.138
Hey there, bud.

00:03:39.937 --> 00:03:41.063
Remember me?

00:03:43.399 --> 00:03:45.151
-It's okay.
-[gasps]

00:03:47.612 --> 00:03:48.946
[sniffs]

00:03:49.739 --> 00:03:51.449
-[grunts happily]
-[laughing]

00:03:52.366 --> 00:03:53.534
[laughing]

00:03:55.077 --> 00:03:58.623
Hey, I am glad
to see you, too, bud. [grunts]

00:03:58.706 --> 00:04:00.875
He's not gonna eat your father.

00:04:01.250 --> 00:04:04.086
Hey! How's the tail holding up?

00:04:05.046 --> 00:04:06.714
Probably could use some oil
and a little fine-tuning.

00:04:06.839 --> 00:04:09.634
Look, it's okay. They're friends.

00:04:09.800 --> 00:04:11.177
[laughing]

00:04:11.719 --> 00:04:13.846
[groans] Come on.

00:04:15.389 --> 00:04:16.265
Here.

00:04:16.974 --> 00:04:18.351
Go on. It's all right.

00:04:18.434 --> 00:04:19.393
Come.

00:04:20.353 --> 00:04:21.395
He won't hurt you.

00:04:22.855 --> 00:04:25.191
Hold your hands out. Like this.

00:04:26.943 --> 00:04:27.902
That's it.

00:04:31.697 --> 00:04:33.199
Let him come to you.

00:04:37.578 --> 00:04:39.580
[purring softly]

00:04:39.664 --> 00:04:40.915
[both gasp]

00:04:53.594 --> 00:04:54.845
[Hiccup's son laughs]

00:04:56.973 --> 00:04:58.140
[laughs]

00:05:01.519 --> 00:05:03.145
[Toothless roaring]

00:05:05.564 --> 00:05:07.149
[exclaims]

00:05:11.696 --> 00:05:13.155
[baby dragons chittering]

00:05:22.540 --> 00:05:24.083
[Astrid whoops]

00:05:24.292 --> 00:05:26.002
[Astrid and daughter laugh]

00:05:26.961 --> 00:05:28.045
[Hiccup] Legend says

00:05:28.129 --> 00:05:31.590
that when the ground quakes
or lava spews from the earth,

00:05:31.674 --> 00:05:35.594
it's the dragons
letting us know they're still here.

00:05:36.846 --> 00:05:39.515
Waiting for us to figure out
how to get along.

00:05:44.061 --> 00:05:45.229
[Stormfly squawks]

00:05:48.024 --> 00:05:50.735
Yes, the world believes
the dragons are gone,

00:05:50.818 --> 00:05:52.611
if they ever existed at all.

00:05:53.696 --> 00:05:56.615
But we Berkians, we know otherwise.

00:05:58.159 --> 00:06:01.203
And we'll guard this secret
until the time comes

00:06:01.912 --> 00:06:05.374
when dragons can return in peace.

